   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A function \\( f \\) has derivatives of all orders. The third-degree Taylor polynomial for \\( f \\) about \\( x = 0 \\) is used to approximate \\( f\\left(\\frac{1}{10}\\right) \\). It is known that \\( f^{(4)}(0) = 2 \\) and that \\( |f^{(4)}(x)| \\le 5 \\) for all \\( x \\) between \\( 0 \\) and \\( \\frac{1}{10} \\). Find the Lagrange error bound for this approximation."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         1,
         48000
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 3 polynomial needs the maximum of \\( |f^{(4)}(x)| \\), the derivative of order \\( 4 \\), between the centre and the input.",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The bound is \\( \\frac{M\\,|x - 0|^{4}}{4!} \\) with \\( M = 5 \\) and \\( |x - 0| = \\frac{1}{10} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            48000
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluating gives \\( \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{10}\\right)^{4}}{24} = \\frac{1}{48000} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            48000
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The error is at most \\( \\frac{1}{48000} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            48000
         ]
      }
   ],
